<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazilian Gold Rush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from <a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brazilian Gold Rush was the large-scale exploitation of gold deposits in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minas-gerais">Minas Gerais</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, following discoveries in the 1690s, with diamond finds following after 1729. It produced a spectacular revenue surge for the Portuguese crown and funded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-v-of-portugal">João V</a>'s lavish court. The site treats the reliance on this windfall as part of the story of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>'s decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazilian-gold-rush.jpg" alt="Brazilian Gold Rush" width="233" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rodolfo Amoedo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rodolfo_Amoedo_-_Ciclo_do_Ouro,_Acervo_do_Museu_Paulista_da_USP.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
